uby","state":"uploaded","size":2485,"digest":"sha256:da9423f1a7cbb89f649828ee79854e04c001fc45fb08b569ea094273864253cd","download_count":2,"created_at":"2026-11-20T07:10:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-20T07:10:42Z"},{"id":770843085,"node_id":"RA_kwDOR65CUM4t8iHN","name":"sha256.sum","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":705,"digest":"sha256:ccb82987ab0168a592e5a506348df225d5e0b581d71a8c98c57de2f9305a0435","download_count":3,"created_at":"2026-11-20T07:10:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-20T07:10:42Z"},{"id":770843086,"node_id":"RA_kwDOR65CUM4t8iHO","name":"source.tar.gz","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/x-gtar","state":"uploaded","size":2348755,"digest":"sha256:fe316ac20de9bbd6f17010b6ee49e6f4803978d66c16e41b69e2d5534bb9d607","download_count":3,"created_at":"2026-11-20T07:10:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-20T07:10:42Z"},{"id":770843088,"node_id":"RA_kwDOR65CUM4t8iHQ","name":"source.tar.gz.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":81,"digest":"sha256:cf1aba7dccd2dac19eb592e50f29cbb0b56448185a6aedfcf1b084a4c4233503","download_count":2,"created_at":"2026-11-20T07:10:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-20T07:10:42Z"}],"body":"## Release Notes\n\n### Added\n\n- An **Autosave** toggle on the welcome screen.\n\n### Changed\n\n- Prompts that appear on their own, such as an update notice, a file-changed warning, or diff review opened by an outside change, now ignore keys for a moment so you don't answer them by accident while typing.\n- Diff review opens faster on large files.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Saving a file that mixes `CRLF` and `LF` line endings now asks which one to use instead of silently converting every line.\n- Saving now backs up the file first, so a save that fails partway, such as on a full disk, no longer loses the file's contents.\n- Inline code no longer draws in the same color as its background with `--no-config`, or with a custom theme that leaves out the `code` or `bg` color.\n- `--no-config` now uses the Edamame theme on terminals with 24-bit color, and 256 Dark otherwise.\n- Preview: **Go to section** (`Ctrl-G`) now starts at the section at the top of the screen rather than wherever the cursor was.\n- Preview: `Ctrl-Shift-T` (Insert Table) no longer opens the table prompt, matching other editing shortcuts.\n- Preview: with wrapped lines, the status-bar breadcrumb no longer shows a later heading than the one on screen.\n- Preview: entering edit with the cursor scrolled out of view now places it at the top of the screen. Before, it could land lower down or off screen, and the first keypress made the view jump.\n- Scrolling down with the keyboard inside a long list, quote, table, code block or paragraph no longer sends the cursor back to the start of that block, which made the next keypress jump the view back up.\n- A heading containing a footnote reference now gets the same `#anchor` as on GitHub, in the app and in HTML export, so links to it keep working once published.\n- An HTML comment inside a block of HTML, or on the line right after one (such as after `</details>`), is now dimmed like other comments.\n- Following a link to a missing file now says \"File not found\", and suggests the `.md` file if the link left off the extension. Before, it showed an unclear error, or nothing at all for a Markdown link. A linked Markdown file that can't be read now says why.\n- Text containing recently added characters (Unicode 18) now lines up correctly in tables and wrapped lines.\n- Vim: case-insensitive `:s` patterns with a non-ASCII range (such as `[à-ÿ]`) no longer miss some matches.\n- Vim: a few rare `:s` patterns that combine back-references or lookaround with repetition no longer match the wrong text or crash the editor.\n- Windows: edamame no longer occasionally hangs when it stops watching a file for outside changes, such as when opening another file or quitting.\n\n### Security\n\n- HTML export's sanitizer no longer lets crafted SVG or MathML in a document's raw HTML through into the exported file, where it could run script when the file is opened in a browser (RUSTSEC-2026-0533).\n\n## Install edamame 0.1.8\n\n### Install prebuilt binaries via shell script\n\n```sh\ncurl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -LsSf https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-installer.sh | sh\n```\n\n### Install prebuilt binaries via Homebrew\n\n```sh\nbrew install mijowi/tap/edamame\n```\n\n## Download edamame 0.1.8\n\n|  File  | Platform | Checksum |\n|--------|----------|----------|\n| [edamame-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.xz](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.xz) | Apple Silicon macOS | [checksum](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.xz.sha256) |\n| [edamame-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.xz](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.xz) | Intel macOS | [checksum](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.xz.sha256) |\n| [edamame-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip) | x64 Windows | [checksum](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip.sha256) |\n| [edamame-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz) | ARM64 Linux | [checksum](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz.sha256) |\n| [edamame-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz) | x64 Linux | [checksum](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.xz.sha256) |\n| [edamame-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.xz](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.xz) | x64 MUSL Linux | [checksum](https://github.com/mijowi/edamame/releases/download/v0.1.8/edamame-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.xz.sha256) |\n\n\n"}
